  "question": "If $y = [x^x]^x$ for $x>0$, find $\\frac{dy}{dx}$.",
  "answeroption": "B",
  "explanation": "$y = (x^x)^x = x^{x^2}$.<br /><br />Take logarithm:<br /><br />$\\ln y = x^2 \\ln x$.<br /><br />Differentiate:<br /><br />$\\frac{1}{y}\\frac{dy}{dx} = 2x\\ln x + x$.<br /><br />Therefore,<br /><br />$\\frac{dy}{dx} = x^{x^2}(2x\\ln x + x)$.",
